        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "In the given $x$-order,\n\n$x^2-2x$ gives $8,3,0,-1,0,3,8$.\n\n$2x-x^2$ gives $-8,-3,0,1,0,-3,-8$.",
          "worked": "Substitute each header value into $x^2-2x$. For example,\n$$\\begin{align*}(-2)^2-2(-2)&=4+4\\\\(-2)^2-2(-2)&=8.\\end{align*}$$\nThe first row is $8,3,0,-1,0,3,8$. Since $2x-x^2=-(x^2-2x)$, negate each first-row value to obtain $-8,-3,0,1,0,-3,-8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Sketch the two parabolas and state the vertex of each.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=x^2-2x$ has vertex $(1,-1)$.\n\n$y=2x-x^2$ has vertex $(1,1)$. Both pass through $(0,0)$ and $(2,0)$.",
          "worked": "Plot the table values and join each set with a smooth parabola. The values are symmetric about $x=1$. The upward parabola has minimum point $(1,-1)$, and the downward parabola has maximum point $(1,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p14-q1-c-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"p14 q1c; teacher p32\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.05cm,y=0.85cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-1.1,0)--(3.35,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-3.15)--(0,3.15) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.8pt,domain=-0.95:2.95,samples=100] plot (\\x,{(\\x)^2-2*(\\x)});\n\\draw[<->,dashed,line width=0.8pt,domain=-0.95:2.95,samples=100] plot (\\x,{2*(\\x)-(\\x)^2});\n\\fill (1,-1) circle (1.4pt) (1,1) circle (1.4pt);\n\\node[below,yshift=-4pt] at (1,-1) {$(1,-1)$};\n\\node[above,yshift=4pt] at (1,1) {$(1,1)$};\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (2,0.07)--(2,-0.07);\n\\node[anchor=north west] at (2.4,-0.12) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$2$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
